# Testing and security

## Test setup

- PHPUnit feature tests in `tests/Feature`. `phpunit.xml` uses SQLite `:memory:`, array cache,
  sync queue, array session. Do not change those values or point tests at MySQL.
- Never run tests, seeders, or `migrate:fresh` against the local MySQL `multi_tenant_blog` unless asked.
- Tenant test pattern:

```php
use RefreshDatabase;

protected function tearDown(): void
{
    if (tenancy()->initialized) {
        tenancy()->end();
    }
    Tenant::query()->get()->each(fn (Tenant $tenant) => $tenant->delete());
    parent::tearDown();
}
```

- Use hosts like `http://alpha.localhost` / `http://beta.localhost`; central checks use `http://localhost`.
- Use `$this->withoutVite()` for Inertia page tests; use `Post::forceCreate` to set `user_id` in fixtures.
- Cross-tenant session tests must replay the real session cookie; call `flushSession()` before
  requesting a second tenant host in the same test.

## Every feature or fix must

- Add isolation tests (tenant A cannot read or change tenant B's data, files, cache, or jobs)
  and authorization tests (guests, other writers, non-admins).
- Keep `php artisan test` and `npm run build` passing. Never weaken checks to make a test pass.

## Security expectations

- Validate server-side in Form Requests; enforce ownership with policies.
- Unpublished or missing posts return 404 publicly; drafts have null `published_at`,
  scheduled posts require a future date.
- Uploads: JPEG/PNG/WebP, max 2 MB, generated filenames, tenant-scoped paths, no traversal.
- Branding colors must match `/^#[0-9a-f]{6}$/`; invalid values fall back to defaults.
- Never commit `.env`, credentials, tenant uploads (`storage/tenant*/`), or tenant DB files.
